.Ss June 28, 2026
Confused about different types of pattern matching that can be done.
Globbing and extended globbing are designed for file name matching,
so I am going to use extended regex for the lexer.
.Pp
.Sy Standard Globbing
.Bl -tag -width "[:space:], [:digit:]..." -offset indent
.It Cm *
Any string of characters.
.Ql file*.txt
matches
.Pa file.txt ,
.Pa file1.txt .
.It Cm ?
Exactly one character.
.Ql image?.png
matches
.Pa image1.png ,
.Pa imageA.png .
.It Cm [...]
Any one character, including ranges.
.Ql log_[0-9].txt
matches
.Pa log_0.txt ,
.Pa log_1.txt .
.It Cm [!...]
or
.Cm [^...]
Matches any one character not enclosed in brackets.
.Ql data_[!0-9].csv
matches
.Pa data_a.csv .
.It Cm [:space:] , [:digit:] , [:lower:] , [:upper:] , [:alpha:] , [:alnum:]
POSIX character classes.
.Ql file_[[:digit:]].txt
matches
.Pa file_7.txt .
.El
.Pp
.Sy Extended Globbing
.Pp
Uses a quantifier followed by a list of patterns, separated by OR
.Ql | .
.Bl -tag -width "?(pattern-list)" -offset indent
.It Cm ?(pattern-list)
Zero or ONE occurrence of patterns.
.Ql file?(test).txt
matches
.Pa file.txt
and
.Pa filetest.txt .
.It Cm *(pattern-list)
Zero or MORE occurrences of patterns.
.Ql data*(0).csv
matches
.Pa data0.csv
and
.Pa data000.csv .
.It Cm +(pattern-list)
One or more occurrences.
.Ql track+(0).mp3
matches
.Pa track0.mp3
but won't match
.Pa track.mp3 .
.It Cm @(pattern-list)
Exactly one of the given patterns.
.Ql report.@(pdf|txt).doc
matches
.Pa report.pdf ,
.Pa report.txt
but won't match
.Pa report.jpg .
.It Cm !(pattern-list)
Anything except the given patterns (can be combined).
.El
.Pp
Extended Globbing Examples:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
.Ql '*([0-9])?(.csv)'
finds strings that optionally end with .csv (e.g., 123 and 564.csv).
.It
.Ql rm '!(*.jpg|*.png)'
deletes all files except jpg and png images.
.El
